Local patch for AutoPrimeNet 2.0.2 (apply AFTER
autoprimenet-2.0.2-prime95-report-only.patch and
autoprimenet-2.0.2-untrusted-fetch.patch).

Keep multi-curve ECM assignments open: the stock report_result() always sends
d=1 for ECM curve results, so PrimeNet closes the assignment when the first
curve is reported and every further curve of that assignment is rejected with
"PrimeNet error 43: Invalid assignment key: au: no such assignment key".
mprime writes one worktodo line per curve (curves=1), so the remaining-curve
information is available in `tasks`: send d=0 while another line for the same
(k,b,n,c) is still queued, and d=1 for the last curve (or when a factor was
found).  This is what makes the single-curve farm queue work for ECM.

--- a/autoprimenet.py
+++ b/autoprimenet.py
@@ -8085,7 +8085,27 @@
 		if result_type == PRIMENET_AR.PP1_FACTOR:
 			params["f"] = ",".join(ar["factors"])
 	elif result_type in {PRIMENET_AR.ECM_FACTOR, PRIMENET_AR.ECM_NOFACTOR}:
-		params["d"] = 1
+		# ECM assignments ask for many curves (CR) and mprime writes one
+		# worktodo line per curve, reporting each curve separately.  Keep the
+		# assignment open while more curves for it are still queued; only the
+		# last curve (or a found factor) closes it.  The stock code always sent
+		# d=1, which makes PrimeNet close the assignment after the first curve
+		# and turns all remaining curves into "invalid assignment key" results.
+		if result_type == PRIMENET_AR.ECM_FACTOR:
+			params["d"] = 1
+		else:
+			params["d"] = (
+				0
+				if any(
+					task.k == assignment.k
+					and task.b == assignment.b
+					and task.n == assignment.n
+					and task.c == assignment.c
+					for task in tasks
+					if isinstance(task, Assignment)
+				)
+				else 1
+			)
 		params.update((("A", assignment.k), ("b", assignment.b), ("c", assignment.c)))
 		params["CR"] = ar["curves"]
 		params["B1"] = ar["b1"]
